  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-PMR26-TLS101</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved evidence based policy formulation and advocacy to support youth employment and training in the country</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Timor-Leste faces ongoing development challenges, including high youth unemployment, limited economic opportunities, especially in rural areas, and a disconnect between training systems and labour market needs. Women and youth are particularly vulnerable to unemployment and underemployment. The country&apos;s Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET) system is currently unable to adequately meet labour market demands, especially in agroforestry.

To address this, the ILO, is supporting sustainable economic growth and decent job creation through improved skills development and labour market integration in selected value chains. This initiative is implemented in close coordination with relevant ministries, training institutions, private sector representatives, trade unions, and the employer organisation. 

The ILO also assists the National Employment Strategy Secretariat of the Secretariat of State for Vocational Training and Employment, in developing an action-oriented implementation plan, detailing responsibilities, timelines, and resource needs.</narrative>
  </description>
